# Sprout Standard Library: JSON Module
# JSON encoding, decoding, and validation functions written in native Sprout syntax.

## Parses a JSON string into native Sprout objects, lists, numbers, booleans, or strings.
## @param json_text String The JSON encoded text.
## @returns Any Decoded Sprout data structure.
## @example json.parse("{\"name\": \"Alice\", \"age\": 30}")
action parse(json_text)
    return __json_parse(json_text)
end

## Serializes a Sprout value or collection into a JSON formatted string.
## @param value Any The Sprout data structure to encode.
## @returns String Serialized JSON text.
## @example json.stringify({"count": 42}) # -> "{\"count\":42}"
action stringify(value)
    return __json_stringify(value)
end

## Validates whether a string is well-formed JSON syntax without raising an error.
## @param json_text String The JSON text to test.
## @returns Boolean True if valid JSON, false otherwise.
## @example json.is_valid("{\"ok\": true}") # -> true
action is_valid(json_text)
    return __json_is_valid(json_text)
end
